From 2742cbeb54638e0939c3acb6647c0f90dab8a417 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 13:36:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] configure: require vec_splats in the AltiVec intrinsics
 probe

The AltiVec kernels use vec_splats, the one intrinsic they rely on
outside the original AltiVec PIM.  Apple's GCC 4.x accepts the rest
under -faltivec but does not provide vec_splats, so the probe passed
and the build then failed later in celt_altivec.c.  Call vec_splats
from the probe body so such a compiler fails the check and falls back
to the C path instead.

Verified with the powerpc-linux-gnu cross toolchain: -mcpu=7450 passes
with empty OPUS_PPC_ALTIVEC_CFLAGS, the flagless build still picks up
-maltivec -mabi=altivec, and a simulated missing vec_splats yields
intrinsics_support=no with OPUS_PPC_MAY_HAVE_ALTIVEC and
OPUS_PPC_PRESUME_ALTIVEC both undefined.  Regenerate configure before
building from a checkout (autogen.sh / autoreconf).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 configure.ac | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
index 69e2e708..83bd5c3e 100644
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -790,7 +790,9 @@ AS_IF([test x"$enable_intrinsics" = x"yes"],[
                static __vector float A0, A1;
                __vector float SUMM;
                float res[[4]] __attribute__((aligned(16)));
-               SUMM = vec_madd(A0, A1, A0);
+               /* vec_splats is the one non-PIM intrinsic the kernels use;
+                  compilers without it (Apple GCC 4.x) must fail this probe. */
+               SUMM = vec_madd(A0, A1, vec_splats(0.5f));
                vec_st(SUMM, 0, res);
                return (int)res[[0]];
             ]]
@@ -810,7 +812,9 @@ AS_IF([test x"$enable_intrinsics" = x"yes"],[
                   static __vector float A0, A1;
                   __vector float SUMM;
                   float res[[4]] __attribute__((aligned(16)));
-                  SUMM = vec_madd(A0, A1, A0);
+                  /* vec_splats is the one non-PIM intrinsic the kernels use;
+                     compilers without it (Apple GCC 4.x) must fail this probe. */
+                  SUMM = vec_madd(A0, A1, vec_splats(0.5f));
                   vec_st(SUMM, 0, res);
                   return (int)res[[0]];
                ]]
